WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.091
Validation evaluates both the source and the specific information it provides.

00:00:05.091 --> 00:00:12.217
Ask who created the material, when, with what access and expertise, and for what possible purpose.

00:00:12.217 --> 00:00:19.752
A credible publisher can make an error, while an unfamiliar source may provide a verifiable primary artifact.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:23.620
Distinguish primary sources, secondary analysis, and recycled reporting.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:31.562
Primary material is closest to the event or official record, but it may still be incomplete or self-interested.

00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:35.023
Secondary sources can add expertise and context.

00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:39.299
Recycled claims can create the illusion of broad agreement.

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:42.761
Corroboration means independent evidence supports a claim.

00:00:42.761 --> 00:00:47.444
Ten articles repeating one anonymous statement are not ten confirmations.

00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:54.571
Trace assertions to their origin and seek sources with different access paths, methods, or evidence types.

00:00:54.571 --> 00:00:58.033
Examine timeliness, bias, manipulation, and internal consistency.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.273
Infrastructure and roles change.

00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:03.327
Images can be genuine but miscaptioned.

00:01:03.327 --> 00:01:09.232
Old records can accurately describe a past state while misleading a current assessment.

00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:14.323
Look for credible contradictory evidence and document how conflicts were resolved.

00:01:14.323 --> 00:01:16.563
Use confidence language consistently.

00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:20.839
Confidence reflects source quality, corroboration, consistency, and remaining gaps.

00:01:20.839 --> 00:01:29.594
It is not the same as impact or urgency, and it should not be inflated because a conclusion feels plausible.

00:01:29.594 --> 00:01:32.649
When evidence remains unresolved, say so.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:38.554
Reporting an unverified claim with clear limitations is more useful than forcing certainty.

00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:47.310
Record what additional evidence would raise or lower confidence and whether the requirement can be answered responsibly with available sources.
